      "message": "I would use BroadcastRadioFactory* .\n\nThe problem with the way you have it is that the sp\u003c\u003e is used as an argument to operator-\u003e, which converts it to a raw pointer, which is then converted back to an sp\u003c\u003e by registerAsService(). Generating two sp\u003c\u003es from the same native pointer is generally bad practice. (For std::shared_ptr, it would be a clear bug.) It works here because their lifetimes are guaranteed to overlap, and they\u0027ll use the same reference count. But what looks like a simplification here actually makes reasoning about the code considerably more complicated.\n\nI\u0027m not a fan of registerAsService()-like APIs that convert an incoming this pointer to an sp\u003c\u003e. But I presume that can\u0027t be changed?",
